{
  "schema_version": "temple.work-item/v1",
  "id": "WI-0047",
  "title": "Make Temple Workspace human-first and fluid across screen sizes",
  "state": "release_gate",
  "owner_position": "release_manager",
  "assigned_agent_id": "agent-mog",
  "created_at": "2026-08-31T01:59:38.303Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-31T02:31:00.561Z",
  "scope": [
    "Reframe the existing private management surface as Temple Workspace, replace system-centric labels and numeric navigation with human-facing names and semantic icons, add light and dark themes, and make the shell fluid across ultrawide desktop, laptop, tablet, and mobile while preserving canonical data, privacy, and local-command boundaries."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The visible product and destination names use Temple Workspace, Overview, Team, Work, Usage, Health, and Activity; internal technical terminology remains available only where it adds traceability.",
    "Primary navigation uses accessible semantic icons and visible labels, becomes an icon rail on tablet widths, and becomes an accessible drawer on mobile without numeric prefixes.",
    "At 3440, 2560, 1440, 1024, 768, and 390 CSS-pixel widths the page has no horizontal overflow and uses available wide-screen space for meaningful content columns.",
    "Light and dark themes respect the first system preference, can be changed explicitly, and persist locally without changing project or command state.",
    "Private-viewer redaction, read-only behavior, one-snapshot refresh semantics, and loopback-only Human Inbox and Agent Commands remain unchanged.",
    "Focused tests, full verification, and independent browser QA pass on the exact candidate revision before the work stops at Release Gate."
  ],
